Based on the definition of the derivative, find \( f^{\prime}(0) \):

\[ f(x) = \left\{ \begin{array}{cc} 
x^{2} \cos \left(\frac{4}{3 x}\right) + \frac{x^{2}}{2}, & x \neq 0 \\ 
0, & x = 0 
\end{array} 
\right. \]

Let \( p \) be a prime number, \( n \) be a positive integer, and \( n = n_0 + n_1 p + n_2 p^2 + \cdots + n_i p^t \), where \( n_i \in \mathbb{N}^*, 0 \leq n_i \leq p-1, i=0,1,2, \cdots, t \). Let \( S_n \) denote the set of ordered triples \( (a, b, c) \) that satisfy the following conditions:
1. \( a, b, c \) are non-negative integers;
2. \( a + b + c = n \);
3. \( \frac{n!}{a!b!c!} \) is not divisible by \( p \).

How many ordered triples \( (a, b, c) \) are in the set \( S_n \)?

Consider the sequence of numbers \( x_{1}, x_{2}, \ldots, x_{2015} \). Given the following conditions:

\[ 
x_{n}= \begin{cases}
7, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 9 \text{ and } 32 ; \\ 
9, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 7 \text{ and } 32 ; \\
32, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 7 \text{ and } 9 ; \\
0, & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]

Find the sum of all terms in this sequence.

Given the equations \(x^{2}+b x+c=0\) and \(x^{2}+c x+b=0\), both of which have two integer roots \(x_{1}, x_{2}\) and \(x^{\prime}_{1}, x^{\prime}_{2}\) respectively, and \(x_{1} x_{2} > 0\), \(x^{\prime}_{1} x^{\prime}_{2} > 0\).

(1) Prove that \(x_{1} < 0\) and \(x_{2} < 0\);

(2) Prove that \(b-1 \leqslant c \leqslant b+1\);

(3) Find all possible values of \(b\) and \(c\).

Based on the definition of the derivative, find \( f^{\prime}(0) \):

$$
f(x)=\left\{
\begin{array}{c}
2 x^{2}+x^{2} \cos \frac{1}{x}, \quad x \neq 0 \\
0, \quad x=0
\end{array}
\right.
$$
